  "jp1": {
    "header": "JP1",
    "rows": 13,
    "note": "Physical pin per assigned signal. Twelve header GPIOs carry eleven signals, so GPIO35 on JP1 15 is spare and must stay unconnected: it is the ESP32-P4 serial-bootloader strap. JP1 21 / GPIO28 was FLASH_EN under ECN-0002 and carries BTN_SHUTTER since ECN-0003 (2026-08-30), which dropped the built-in flash from D4-V1 for a separate external module with no P4 pin; the signal count is still eleven. GPIO28 is not a strapping pin (those are GPIO34-38), which is why a switch to ground is safe there and would not be on JP1 15. Firmware source of truth: firmware/p4/main/board_d4v1.h BOARD_*_JP1; test_board_pins.c --dump generates these values.",
